   723	### 6.2 Issuance window (C4 verifier rule)
   724	
   725	- The window `issuance-not-after − issuance-not-before` is at most 90 days. A record that violates it is rejected
   726	  (`DNS_WINDOW_LENGTH`). V1 has one window and no overlap. [A9:409-411; ENC §7:578-580]
   727	- A receipt is `INVALID / ISSUANCE_WINDOW` unless `issuance-not-before` ≤ declared issue time and T ≤
   728	  `issuance-not-after`. Both bounds are inclusive. T is compared as registered, with no margin. T is not compared
   729	  with not-before. [A9:419-421; ENC §7.1:636-643, 662-663]
   730	- The guarantee is in chain time. A UTC cutoff would need a backward-skew bound V1 does not establish. [A9:441-447;
   731	  ENC §7.1:661-671]
   732	- A published window cannot be shortened. [A9:424]
   733	- The window, its dates and the stop margin are operating facts, not profile rules. [A9:422-423; RB §2]
