  1190	## 10. Number rule
  1191	
  1192	Accept a number exactly when RFC 8785's canonical serialization preserves its value. Reject otherwise. The three
  1193	conditions (not negative zero, finite after round-half-even, exact decimal value of `ES(d)` equals the literal) and
  1194	the accepted and rejected examples are in ENC §1.2. [A9:519-524; ENC §1.2:118-148; ENC D-1:752-755] Proof:
  1195	`formal/p8/PROOF.md` Lemma 3. Vectors: `formal/p8/vectors/`.
  1196	
  1197	This replaces the literal "exactly representable as an IEEE 754 double" rule for this profile only. [A9:486-487;
  1198	A9:521-524] The stale "needs an author sentence" remarks in ENC (ENC:147-148, D-1) and PROOF §6 are superseded by
  1199	A9.8. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G38; the ENC and PROOF wording edits are done, OWNER 2026-10-19]
  1200	
  1201	**`ES` recipe.** `ES(d)` is ECMA-262 NumberToString (7.1.12.1, Note 2) of the 10th edition (June 2019), the edition RFC 8785 cites
  1202	(edition, section and digest in the dependency manifest; later editions rename it Number::toString with the same
  1203	output) [OWNER 2026-10-19, item 15; source formal/dependency-sources/MANIFEST.md]. If d is +0 or −0: `"0"`. If d < 0: `"-"` ‖ ES(−d). Otherwise let n, k, s be integers with
  1204	k ≥ 1, 10^(k−1) ≤ s < 10^k, s × 10^(n−k) = d as a double, and k as small as possible; if several s qualify, choose
  1205	the one for which s × 10^(n−k) is closest in value to d, and if two are equally close, the even one. Then: if
  1206	k ≤ n ≤ 21, the k digits followed by n−k zeros; if 0 < n ≤ 21, the first n digits, `.`, the remaining k−n digits;
  1207	if −6 < n ≤ 0, `0.`, −n zeros, the digits; otherwise the first digit, then `.` and the remaining digits if k > 1,
  1208	then `e`, `+` or `-`, and abs(n−1) in decimal. Any formatter must reproduce N-01…N-22 and C-N01…C-N22; Python's
  1209	`repr` is not ES. Unicode tables must be 16.0.0, identified by the UCD file digests in the dependency manifest; a
  1210	runtime may use bundled pinned tables, and one whose tables do not match refuses to run (no verdict).
  1211	[OWNER 2026-10-14, G29]
  1212	
  1213	**Field grammars.** `utc` years run 0001–9999 (proleptic Gregorian, seconds 00–59). LDH labels match
  1214	`[a-z0-9-]{1,63}` with no leading or trailing hyphen; all-numeric labels, the top label included, are allowed; at
  1215	least two labels; at most 241 bytes. This is what both P8 codecs already do. [OWNER 2026-10-14, G18; the ENC §3.2
  1216	and §7 wording edit is done, OWNER 2026-10-19]
  1217	
