   780	(:267-283), since `utc_assessment` is outside the stable six; A9's "no lower time bound or priority" (:46-47); A8.3
   781	and A8.5, which supply no evidence for option (e); A9.6's issuer invariant and guarantee 2's body, its chain-time
   782	meaning and its capture proviso; A9's public-publication issuer duty ("Changed in effect", :495-500); the scenario
   783	mapping's verdicts, fixtures and safe-decision categories. `docs/V1-PROFILE.md` is not changed by this amendment:
   784	A10.5 states its existing order, and the profile changes that rows 20–39 would need (memo, Part 3, "Minimal spec and
   785	verifier changes") are made after this amendment's signing commit. A1.6 (:485-505) stays standing: its clock wording is
   786	qualified for V1 by A10.1, and its parenthetical "a reorganization deeper than k is out of model" uses the same
   787	phrase as rows 13–14, while its governing clause ("anchors at depth ≥ k are treated as permanent") already matches
   788	A10.3. A9's header still reads "PROPOSED"; its signing act is commit `2ad3489` under the house form, and this
   789	amendment does not change that.
   790	
   791	**In sum:** thirty-nine rows. Rows 1–14 and 17–19 are OWNER DECISIONS and add no mechanism. Rows 15–16 and 20–39 are
   792	AUTHOR ADOPTED (2026-10-18). By kind: fifteen narrow claims (rows 1–11, 13–16), one correction to the registered
   793	encoding (row 19), five clarifications (rows 12, 17, 18, 23, 24), thirteen broadenings (rows 20–22, 25–31, 37–39)
   794	and five gate changes (rows 32–36; row 33 also states its scope change). The broadenings add mechanism: one reported
   795	assessment and one named assumption (A10.1.1); one trust-file field, the tuple classifier and the ordered listing
   796	subchecks, four reason codes, closure invariants, release stamping, the listing-evidence package and one issuer
   797	invariant (A10.4.1). The scenario mapping's verdicts are unchanged; option (e) deliberately rejects new cases:
   798	receipts under unlisted keys, and receipts whose listing was not pre-committed. No existing verdict, parameter or
   799	vector is changed; the existing header checks extend to the installed listing headers (A10.4.1).
